<guide>

    Follow this guide to add a new prayer line to play when playing a
    particular character with Giygas in the SPNatI April Fool’s event.

    Do all of the below in Giygas's behaviour.xml file
    (spnati/opponents/giygas/behaviour.xml).

<!--
==STEP 1==
    Use this template to create the prayer line case.
    It’s a complicated set of conditions, so you’ll have an easier time
    just copy-and-pasting into behaviour.xml than you would using the
    CE for this.
-->

            <case stage="1-4" priority="750">
                    <!-- 750 is the default priority, but it can be changed if you want the
                         prayer to only play after more "common" ones so it can act as a
                         punchline. Here is the full list:
                         - 760: Kumatora only (potentially another major Earthbound character if one's added)
                         - 751: Friendname is somehow very close to or already actively watching Giygas (i.e. Frisk & Friends, Streaming-chan)
                         - 750: Common cases
                         - 749: Uncommon/punchline cases, such as Friendname being antagonistic or unlikely character (e.g. Trigon praying for Raven)
                         - 748: Very uncommon/extra-punchline cases (e.g. Friendname praying for everyone else's safety from Charname)
                         - 747: Prayer fails outright (i.e. Saki Yoshida, Wendy)
                         - 746: Sans only -->
                <condition count="0" filter="charname's_source_tag" character="friendname" />
                    <!-- Checks to make sure Friendname isn't actually in the game.
                         If Friendname is multiple people or has multiple likely filenames
                         if they were to be added, include all of them.
                         Friendname is the character referenced in the actual text of this line. -->
                <condition role="opp" character="charname" />
                    <!-- Charname is the character who triggers this line, and whom Friendname prays for.
                         Replace all instances of "charname" with the character's name,
                         including in marker names. -->
                <condition role="self" saidMarker="PG_ready" notSaidMarker="PG_cut" />
                <condition role="self" notSaidMarker="P_charname" />
                    <!-- These three marker conditions control when the line plays. -->
                <state img="custom:#-prayer" marker="P_charname" direction="none" set-intelligence="throw">
                    <text>{eb}•(This is what the narrator says when Friendname suddenly felt strange,&lt;br&gt;•and began praying for Charname and their friends.&lt;br&gt;){!reset}</text>
                    <!-- {eb} is the Earthbound text window style.
                         The • character is Unicode character 2022.
                         The first • goes before the ( parenthesis, but nothing comes after the
                         ) parenthesis except {!reset}.-->
                    <markers>
                        <marker name="PG_cut" op="=" value="1" />
                        <marker name="PG_scenes" op="+" value="1" />
                        <!-- Can add <marker name="P_charname_variantB" value="1"> if this is a special
                             variant of the prayer scene (e.g. someone actually put Friendname in spnati
                             and you have to work around that). -->
                    </markers>
                </state>
            </case>

<!--            
    Paste this entire case underneath the codeline where it says
    '<trigger id="global">' in giygas/behaviour.xml.
    (Its position in the document doesn't matter as long as it's AFTER
    '<trigger id="global">' and BEFORE the next '</trigger>'.
    The CE will also sort the lines automatically every time it's used.)
-->

<!--
==STEP 2==
    Use this template to create the line that counts for the hook collectible.
-->

            <case stage="1-4" id="1230" hidden="1" priority="-1">
                <condition role="self" saidMarker="P_charname" notSaidMarker="PP_charname" />
                <!-- You still need to replace all instances of "charname"
                     with Charname's actual name. -->
                <test expr="~self.collectible.giygas_hook~" value="false" />
                <state marker="PP_charname">
                    <text>Prayer recorded</text>
                    <markers>
                        <marker name="PG_pcount" op="+" value="1" />
                    </markers>
                </state>
            </case>

<!--            
    Paste this entire case underneath the case from Step 1 in behaviour.xml.
    (Just like the Step 1 case, its position in the document only needs
    to be between '<trigger id="global">' and the next '</trigger>'.)
-->

<!--
==STEP 3==
    Paste this codeline under '<persistent-markers>' in behaviour.xml.
-->
        <marker>PP_charname</marker>
        <!-- You still need to replace "charname" with Charname's actual name. -->

<!--
    Congratulations! If you've just done all of the above,
    you've added a new prayer scene to Giygas!
-->
